Day 31 (2026-10-20 .. 2026-10-22) - VersariteViewer 1.2, the Lab's round trip
with Fiji

The work of these days was done in a second chat; this log was written
afterwards (2026-10-22) from the code, the release notes and Readme_Lab.md.
The unit headers written then call these days "Day 27", "Day 28" and
"Day 29" (the second chat's own count); in this log's count they are
Day 31.

VersariteViewer 1.2 (MViewVersion = '1.2'; docs\release_notes_v1.2.0.md)

1. Slide show (right-click "Slide show (this folder; Esc ends it)",
   command SlideShow): the current folder round and round in the viewer's
   order, each image [Sort] DirPreviewDelayMs counted from when it is on
   screen; a step shows the next at once and the show goes on; Esc ends it
   first; it waits for an unsaved image or edit mode, and gives way to the
   Total Commander dir preview.
2. The speed live: commands DirPreviewLonger / DirPreviewShorter, by
   [Sort] DirPreviewStepMs (100), for the slide show and the dir preview;
   written to the ini at once.
3. The Total Commander dir preview as a slide show: [Sort] TCSlideShowMode
   (command SlideShowMode) keeps the folder under TC's cursor playing
   while VersariteViewer has the focus; command DirPreview switches the
   dir preview.
4. Testers' reports:
   - the X button (Alt+F4, the taskbar's Close) sends the program to the
     taskbar; [Window] CloseButtonMinimizes=0 = the old X;
   - an unsaved crop / paste / filtered copy (and an image from Fiji) is
     not left by the first step of the wheel: "kept"; the wheel again
     after a pause of 0.6 s (within 6 s) leaves it; [Navigation]
     GuardUnsavedCopy;
   - Ctrl+Z = Undo (fixed keys now: Esc, arrows, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Z);
     Undo is the menu's first entry, always there (greyed when empty);
   - Rapid Sorting folders of one's own: [Sort] RapidFolder1 .. 0 (a full
     path, or a name in DefaultImageFolder; empty = Selection<n>);
     TSortFolders.SetRapid takes the ten folders (TConfig.RapidFolder);
   - a double-click on the title bar opens the settings screen;
   - "Magnifier (lens)" back in the right-click menu (hidden by mistake).
5. The aiming loupe: in edit mode, and while a Lab tool places a point,
   the mouse resting [Magnifier] AimRestMs (500) shows a small lens (x4)
   centred on the point with a fine cross; it goes 1 s after a release,
   on a fast move, off the view or over a panel. [Magnifier] AimLoupe=0:
   never. Not with the magnifier on.
6. New settings, all written at the first start and explained on the
   settings screen: [Sort] DirPreviewStepMs, TCSlideShowMode,
   RapidFolder1..0; [Navigation] GuardUnsavedCopy; [Window]
   CloseButtonMinimizes; [Magnifier] AimLoupe, AimRestMs. New commands:
   SlideShow, DirPreview, SlideShowMode, DirPreviewLonger,
   DirPreviewShorter.
7. Core plug-in points (uExtensions) for the Lab: ShowImageInViewer (an
   edition shows a bitmap as a new image, as a crop), the aiming loupe
   (ShowAimLoupe / HideAimLoupe), the edition's Undo joined with the
   viewer's (RegisterEditionUndo, NextUndoStamp: Undo takes back what came
   last), TBurnInMap.ViewScale (burned-in marks look as on screen).

Versarite Image Lab 0.2 (Readme_Lab.md)

8. To Fiji: "Save original to Fiji" (the image's own pixels, for
   analysis; the measuring lines go along as line selections in Fiji's ROI
   Manager, "Line 1: 56.32 µm") and "Save screen to Fiji" (as shown,
   filters, turn and marks burned in, '_screen'). Both calibrated TIFFs.
9. The link (uFijiChannel, fiji\Versarite_Lab_Link.js): Fiji's own
   single-instance listener is not started by the 2025 launcher, so the
   Lab installs a small script into <Fiji>\scripts\Plugins\AutoRun\ that
   listens on 127.0.0.1:57317: PING, OPEN <file>, EVAL <macro> (errors
   with ImageJ's message, the line and the Log). Images go to the Fiji
   already running; the first time the Lab starts Fiji (a second request
   within a minute waits).
10. Back from Fiji: Plugins > Versarite > Send to Versarite Lab
   (fiji\Send_to_Versarite_Lab.js) sends Fiji's image as shown,
   calibrated, to the Lab running (its path in
   %TEMP%\VersariteImageLab\VersariteImageLab.path).
11. Fiji as the engine: "Run in Fiji ..." (uFijiRun): a favourite ImageJ
   macro line (editable; [FijiCommands] Name=macro, "Remember") runs on
   the image's own pixels in batch mode, without Fiji windows, on a thread
   (the Lab stays usable); the result comes back as a new image with the
   parent's scale; Fiji's error and Log are shown; the user's own images
   in Fiji are not touched.
12. Marks:
   - remembered per image for the session (uMarkMemory): the measuring
     lines, scale bar and labels come back with their image;
   - undoable (uMarkUndo), in the viewer's Undo and Ctrl+Z;
   - their look in the left panel (uMarkStylePanel): Color, Font (and
     Bold), Size rows while a mark tool is on; kept as [ScaleBar] Color /
     Font / FontSize / Bold;
   - drawn plain (single lines, text without outline or box), in their
     own colour (white by default), the same on screen, in copies and in
     the SVG.

